### 1. Sign up (should give 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "dateOfBirth": "2003-05-17",
  "pan": "ABCDE1234F"
}

### 2. Same email again (should give 409 ALREADY_EXISTS)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Someone Else",
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "dateOfBirth": "2001-01-01",
  "pan": "ZZZZZ9999Z"
}

### 3. Bad PAN and bad email (should give 400 INVALID_INPUT)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Data",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "password123",
  "dateOfBirth": "2001-01-01",
  "pan": "12345"
}

### 4. Under 18 (should give 400 INVALID_INPUT)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Young User",
  "email": "young@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "dateOfBirth": "2012-01-01",
  "pan": "YOUNG1234Y"
}

### 5. Me without login (should give 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 6. Wrong password (should give 401 "Invalid email or password")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test1@example.com", "password": "wrongpassword" }

### 7. Login (should give 200 with balance)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test1@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### 8. Me after login (should give 200, same balance)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 9. Logout (should give 204)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout

### 10. Me after logout (should give 401 again)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 11. All quotes (log in first)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/quotes

### 12. One quote
GET http://localhost:8080/api/quotes/RELIANCE

### 13. Login as a demo user (owns shares already)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo1@paisafollows.test", "password": "password123" }

### 14. Market BUY 2 RELIANCE (expect 201, status FILLED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "RELIANCE", "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "quantity": 2 }

### 15. Market SELL 1 RELIANCE (expect 201, FILLED, with realisedPnl)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "RELIANCE", "side": "SELL", "type": "MARKET", "quantity": 1 }

### 16. Sell more than owned (expect 422 INSUFFICIENT_QTY)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "RELIANCE", "side": "SELL", "type": "MARKET", "quantity": 5000 }

### 17. Buy far too much (expect 422 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS, and a ROLLBACK in the log)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "MARUTI", "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "quantity": 100000 }

### 18. Unknown stock (expect 404)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "NOTASTOCK", "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "quantity": 1 }

### 19. Order history, page 1 (5 per page)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders?page=0&size=5

### 20. Only rejected orders
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders?status=REJECTED

### 21. Balance after trading
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 22. Login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo1@paisafollows.test", "password": "password123" }

### 23. Current price of RELIANCE (note it as P)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/quotes/RELIANCE

### 24. LIMIT BUY far below P (stays OPEN, money reserved). Use about P minus 10%
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "RELIANCE", "side": "BUY", "type": "LIMIT", "quantity": 2, "price": 1200 }

### 25. Balance: reservedBalance went up
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 26. Open orders
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders?status=OPEN

### 27. Cancel it (paste the orderId from test 24)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/orders/PASTE-ORDER-ID-HERE

### 28. LIMIT BUY above P (fills on the next tick at the tick price, leftover returned). Use about P plus 5%
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "RELIANCE", "side": "BUY", "type": "LIMIT", "quantity": 1, "price": 1500 }

### 29. STOP_LOSS SELL with trigger just below P (fills within a minute or two as the price wanders). Use about P minus 0.2%
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "RELIANCE", "side": "SELL", "type": "STOP_LOSS", "quantity": 1, "triggerPrice": 1410 }

### 30. Basket: leg 2 is far too expensive, so ONLY leg 2 rolls back
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders/basket
Content-Type: application/json

{ "legs": [
    { "symbol": "INFY",   "side": "BUY", "quantity": 1 },
    { "symbol": "MARUTI", "side": "BUY", "quantity": 100000 },
    { "symbol": "TCS",    "side": "BUY", "quantity": 1 }
] }

### 31. History: see FILLED, CANCELLED, REJECTED together
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders?page=0&size=10

### 32. Login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo1@paisafollows.test", "password": "password123" }

### 33. Portfolio (view + function + aggregates)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/portfolio

### 34. Statement, last 30 days (stored procedure)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/statement

### 35. Statement for a date range
GET http://localhost:8080/api/statement?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31

### 36. Buy 1 INFY, so the wallet changes and the trigger fires
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "INFY", "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "quantity": 1 }

### 37. Balance history (written by the trigger)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/wallet/history?limit=5
